-- Tests for nz-part3-publication.l4 (ss 67 to 83A).
-- Every expected value was decided by reading the section quoted beside it BEFORE the module was run.

§ `Section 67 -- What legislation is drafted by PCO`

-- src:462 | The main functions of the PCO, in relation to drafting legislation, are—
-- src:463 | to draft Government Bills and amendments to them; and
-- src:464 | to advise on, or assist with, the drafting of local Bills and private Bills and amendments to them; and
-- src:465 | to draft Members’ Bills, and amendments to them, if the Attorney-General directs; and
-- src:466 | to draft the following:
-- src:467 | any secondary legislation made by Order in Council (unless the Attorney-General otherwise directs):
-- src:468 | any secondary legislation that amends an Act:
-- src:469 | any secondary legislation if the administering agency and the Chief Parliamentary Counsel agree:
-- src:470 | any secondary legislation if the Attorney-General directs; and
-- src:471 | to draft, or advise on or assist in the drafting of, any other legislation that the Attorney-General directs.
#ASSERT `it is a main drafting function of the PCO` `Government Bills and amendments to them` `when` FALSE `or the Attorney-General otherwise directs:` FALSE `or the agency and the Chief Parliamentary Counsel agree:` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `it is a main drafting function of the PCO` `local Bills and private Bills and amendments to them (to advise on or assist with)` `when` FALSE `or the Attorney-General otherwise directs:` FALSE `or the agency and the Chief Parliamentary Counsel agree:` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `it is a main drafting function of the PCO` `Members' Bills and amendments to them` `when` TRUE `or the Attorney-General otherwise directs:` FALSE `or the agency and the Chief Parliamentary Counsel agree:` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
