#ASSERT `the Inland Revenue Department is authorised to draft the Bill` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the Inland Revenue Department is authorised to draft the Bill` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the Inland Revenue Department is authorised to draft the Bill` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the Inland Revenue Department is authorised to draft the Bill` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `an Order in Council authorising the Inland Revenue Department to draft Bills is secondary legislation` EQUALS TRUE

§ `Section 69 -- PCO must publish all legislation`

-- src:481 | The PCO must publish—
-- src:482 | all introduced Bills (and those amendments to Bills that the Attorney-General directs); and
-- src:483 | all Acts; and
-- src:484 | all secondary legislation drafted by the PCO; and
-- src:485 | minimum legislative information for all secondary legislation drafted by the PCO.
#ASSERT `the PCO must publish` `an introduced Bill` `when` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the PCO must publish` `an amendment to a Bill` `when` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the PCO must publish` `an amendment to a Bill` `when` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the PCO must publish` `an Act` `when` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the PCO must publish` `secondary legislation drafted by the PCO` `when` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the PCO must publish` `minimum legislative information for secondary legislation drafted by the PCO` `when` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the PCO must publish` `secondary legislation not drafted by the PCO` `when` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the PCO must publish` `secondary legislation not drafted by the PCO` `when` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- src:486 | The PCO must also notify the making of that secondary legislation by publishing the information required by regulations in the Gazette.
#ASSERT `the PCO must notify the making in the Gazette of` `secondary legislation drafted by the PCO` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the PCO must notify the making in the Gazette of` `an Act` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the PCO must notify the making in the Gazette of` `an introduced Bill` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the PCO must notify the making in the Gazette of` `secondary legislation not drafted by the PCO` EQUALS FALSE

-- src:487 | The PCO may also publish secondary legislation that was not drafted by the PCO as if it were drafted by the PCO. In that case,—
-- src:488 | subsections (1)﻿(d) and (2) apply; and
-- src:489 | section 71 (how and when legislation must be published by PCO) applies; and
-- src:490 | any obligation under any other legislation for the secondary legislation to be published or notified in the Gazette is treated as satisfied.
#ASSERT `an obligation under other legislation to publish or notify the secondary legislation in the Gazette is treated as satisfied` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `an obligation under other legislation to publish or notify the secondary legislation in the Gazette is treated as satisfied` TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `an obligation under other legislation to publish or notify the secondary legislation in the Gazette is treated as satisfied` FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE

§ `Section 70 -- PCO must publish consolidations of legislation that is amended`

-- src:492 | The PCO must publish consolidations of—
-- src:493 | all Acts that are amended; and
-- src:494 | all secondary legislation drafted by the PCO that is amended.
-- src:495 | A consolidation must incorporate the amendments made to the legislation so that it shows the law as at its stated date.
-- src:496 | The consolidation may also show the law as it would be amended by amendments that have not yet commenced if it clearly indicates that those amendments have not yet commenced.
#ASSERT `the PCO must publish a consolidation` TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the PCO must publish a consolidation` FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the PCO must publish a consolidation` FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `a consolidation may show amendments that have not yet commenced` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `a consolidation may show amendments that have not yet commenced` TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `a consolidation may show amendments that have not yet commenced` FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE

§ `Section 71 -- How and when PCO must publish legislation and consolidations of legislation`

-- src:498 | The PCO must electronically publish the following things at the following times:
-- src:499 | What is required to be published
-- src:500 | When it must be published
-- src:501 | Bills
-- src:502 | As soon as practicable after they are introduced
-- src:503 | Amendments to Bills
-- src:504 | As soon as practicable after the amendments are released
-- src:505 | Acts
-- src:506 | As soon as practicable after they are enacted
-- src:507 | Secondary legislation drafted by the PCO
-- src:508 | As soon as practicable after the legislation is made
-- src:509 | Minimum legislative information for secondary legislation drafted by the PCO
-- src:510 | As soon as practicable after the legislation is made
-- src:511 | Consolidations of Acts
-- src:512 | As soon as practicable after the Acts are amended
-- src:513 | Consolidations of secondary legislation that is drafted by the PCO
-- src:514 | As soon as practicable after the legislation is amended
#ASSERT `the event after which the PCO must publish electronically as soon as practicable` `Bills` EQUALS `they are introduced`
#ASSERT `the event after which the PCO must publish electronically as soon as practicable` `Amendments to Bills` EQUALS `the amendments are released`
#ASSERT `the event after which the PCO must publish electronically as soon as practicable` `Acts` EQUALS `they are enacted`
#ASSERT `the event after which the PCO must publish electronically as soon as practicable` `Secondary legislation drafted by the PCO` EQUALS `the legislation is made`
#ASSERT `the event after which the PCO must publish electronically as soon as practicable` `Minimum legislative information for secondary legislation drafted by the PCO` EQUALS `the legislation is made`
#ASSERT `the event after which the PCO must publish electronically as soon as practicable` `Consolidations of Acts` EQUALS `the Acts are amended`
#ASSERT `the event after which the PCO must publish electronically as soon as practicable` `Consolidations of secondary legislation that is drafted by the PCO` EQUALS `the legislation is amended`
-- No number of days anywhere in the section: never a stated latest day.
#ASSERT `the latest day for the PCO to publish electronically` `Bills` `after the event on` (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the latest day for the PCO to publish electronically` `Acts` `after the event on` (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the latest day for the PCO to publish electronically` `Consolidations of Acts` `after the event on` (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS NOTHING

-- src:516 | Legislation or proposed legislation is sufficiently published for the purposes of this Act (for any period during which it is not practicable to publish it electronically) if it is only published and made available in the way set out in subsection (2).
#ASSERT `legislation or proposed legislation is sufficiently published for the period` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `legislation or proposed legislation is sufficiently published for the period` TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `legislation or proposed legislation is sufficiently published for the period` FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- src:517 | Minimum legislative information is sufficiently published for the purposes of this Act if the secondary legislation containing that information (as required at the time of its publication) is published by the PCO under this Act.
#ASSERT `minimum legislative information is sufficiently published` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `minimum legislative information is sufficiently published` FALSE EQUALS FALSE

§ `Section 72 -- How and when electronic versions of legislation must be available on legislation website`

-- src:520 | as far as practicable, legislation published by the PCO under this Act (including official electronic versions of legislation published under section 78) is at all times able to be accessed at, or downloaded from, the legislation website free of charge; and
