§ `Section 79 -- Legal status of official versions`

-- src:577 | An official version of legislation—
-- src:578 | (if it is as originally enacted or made) is taken to correctly set out the text of the legislation; and
-- src:579 | (if it is a consolidation under section 70) is taken to correctly state, as at its stated date, the law enacted or made by the legislation consolidated and by the amendments; and
-- src:580 | (if it is a version of legislation that includes changes made under subpart 2)—
-- src:581 | is taken to correctly state, as at its stated date, the law enacted or made by the legislation and by the changes made (and paragraph (b) also applies if the legislation is also a consolidation); and
-- src:582 | is evidence that those changes are authorised by that subpart.
-- src:584 | The presumptions in this section apply unless the contrary is shown.
#ASSERT `what an official version of that kind is taken to prove` `an official version as originally enacted or made` `unless the contrary is shown:` FALSE EQUALS `It is taken to correctly set out the text of the legislation`
#ASSERT `what an official version of that kind is taken to prove` `an official version that is a consolidation under section 70` `unless the contrary is shown:` FALSE EQUALS `It is taken to correctly state, as at its stated date, the law enacted or made by the legislation consolidated and by the amendments`
#ASSERT `what an official version of that kind is taken to prove` `an official version that includes changes made under subpart 2` `unless the contrary is shown:` FALSE EQUALS `It is taken to correctly state, as at its stated date, the law enacted or made by the legislation and by the changes made, and is evidence that those changes are authorised by subpart 2`
#ASSERT `what an official version of that kind is taken to prove` `an official version that is a consolidation and includes changes made under subpart 2` `unless the contrary is shown:` FALSE EQUALS `It is taken to correctly state, as at its stated date, the law enacted or made by the legislation consolidated and by the amendments (paragraph (b)) and by the changes made (paragraph (c)(i)), and is evidence that those changes are authorised by subpart 2`
#ASSERT `what an official version of that kind is taken to prove` `an official version that is a consolidation and includes changes made under subpart 2` `unless the contrary is shown:` TRUE EQUALS `The presumption does not apply: the contrary is shown`
#ASSERT `what an official version of that kind is taken to prove` `an official version as originally enacted or made` `unless the contrary is shown:` TRUE EQUALS `The presumption does not apply: the contrary is shown`
#ASSERT `what an official version of that kind is taken to prove` `an official version that is a consolidation under section 70` `unless the contrary is shown:` TRUE EQUALS `The presumption does not apply: the contrary is shown`
-- src:583 | An official version of secondary legislation that states the date of publication by the PCO is evidence that the legislation was published on the date stated.
-- src:584 | The presumptions in this section apply unless the contrary is shown.
#ASSERT `an official version is evidence that the secondary legislation was published on the date stated` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `an official version is evidence that the secondary legislation was published on the date stated` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `an official version is evidence that the secondary legislation was published on the date stated` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `an official version is evidence that the secondary legislation was published on the date stated` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

§ `Section 79A -- Legislative status of publication notes and information`

-- src:586 | The following, inserted by the PCO in carrying out its functions of publishing and consolidating legislation, do not form part of the text of the official version of legislation (even if published in that version):
-- src:587 | machine-readable text, links, or other metadata inserted as an aid to assist users of electronic versions of legislation:
-- src:588 | a record of the legislative history of the legislation (including a record of the fact that changes have been made by the PCO under subpart 2):
-- src:589 | information recorded and published by the PCO under clause 14 of Schedule 1 or as an aid to assist users to understand how this Act applies to secondary legislation:
-- src:590 | any other note or information that is clearly identified, in a suitable place on the legislation website, as not forming part of the legislation.
#ASSERT `an item inserted by the PCO forms part of the text of the official version` `machine-readable text, links or other metadata inserted as an aid to users of electronic versions` `when` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `an item inserted by the PCO forms part of the text of the official version` `machine-readable text inserted as an aid to users of electronic versions` `when` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `an item inserted by the PCO forms part of the text of the official version` `links inserted as an aid to users of electronic versions` `when` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `an item inserted by the PCO forms part of the text of the official version` `other metadata inserted as an aid to users of electronic versions` `when` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `an item inserted by the PCO forms part of the text of the official version` `a record of the legislative history of the legislation` `when` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `an item inserted by the PCO forms part of the text of the official version` `a record of the fact that changes have been made by the PCO under subpart 2` `when` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `an item inserted by the PCO forms part of the text of the official version` `information recorded and published under clause 14 of Schedule 1` `when` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `an item inserted by the PCO forms part of the text of the official version` `information published as an aid to understand how this Act applies to secondary legislation` `when` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `an item inserted by the PCO forms part of the text of the official version` `information recorded and published under clause 14 of Schedule 1, or as an aid to understand how this Act applies to secondary legislation` `when` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `an item inserted by the PCO forms part of the text of the official version` `another note or information` `when` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `an item inserted by the PCO forms part of the text of the official version` `another note or information` `when` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 80 -- Evidential status of minimum legislative information`

-- src:593 | Publication of the minimum legislative information for secondary legislation is evidence of the following:
-- src:594 | that the secondary legislation was made; and
-- src:595 | if the date of making is stated, that the secondary legislation was made on that date; and
-- src:596 | if the date of publication of the information is stated with the information, that the information was published on the date stated; and
-- src:597 | if the date of notification of the making of the secondary legislation is stated in the Gazette, that the making of the secondary legislation was notified in the Gazette on the date stated.
-- src:598 | The presumptions in this section apply unless the contrary is shown.
#ASSERT `publication of the minimum legislative information is evidence` `that the secondary legislation was made` `if the date is stated:` FALSE `unless the contrary is shown:` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `publication of the minimum legislative information is evidence` `that the secondary legislation was made on the date stated` `if the date is stated:` TRUE `unless the contrary is shown:` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `publication of the minimum legislative information is evidence` `that the secondary legislation was made on the date stated` `if the date is stated:` FALSE `unless the contrary is shown:` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `publication of the minimum legislative information is evidence` `that the information was published on the date stated` `if the date is stated:` TRUE `unless the contrary is shown:` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `publication of the minimum legislative information is evidence` `that the information was published on the date stated` `if the date is stated:` FALSE `unless the contrary is shown:` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `publication of the minimum legislative information is evidence` `that the making of the secondary legislation was notified in the Gazette on the date stated` `if the date is stated:` TRUE `unless the contrary is shown:` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `publication of the minimum legislative information is evidence` `that the making of the secondary legislation was notified in the Gazette on the date stated` `if the date is stated:` FALSE `unless the contrary is shown:` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `publication of the minimum legislative information is evidence` `that the secondary legislation was made` `if the date is stated:` TRUE `unless the contrary is shown:` TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `publication of the minimum legislative information is evidence` `that the secondary legislation was made on the date stated` `if the date is stated:` TRUE `unless the contrary is shown:` TRUE EQUALS FALSE

§ `Section 81 -- Judicial notice of legislation`

-- src:600 | All courts and persons acting judicially must take judicial notice of all legislation.
#ASSERT `must take judicial notice` TRUE `of` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `must take judicial notice` FALSE `of` TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `must take judicial notice` TRUE `of` FALSE EQUALS FALSE

§ `Section 82 -- Power to revoke spent secondary legislation and other instruments`

-- src:603 | Before making a recommendation, the Attorney-General must be satisfied that the secondary legislation or other instrument has ceased to have effect or is no longer required.
#ASSERT `the Attorney-General may recommend revocation under section 82` TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the Attorney-General may recommend revocation under section 82` FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the Attorney-General may recommend revocation under section 82` FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- src:605 | An order under this section is secondary legislation (see this Part for publication requirements).
#ASSERT `an order under section 82 is secondary legislation` EQUALS TRUE

§ `Section 83 -- Attorney-General directions under this Part`

-- src:608 | The PCO must carry out the functions in this Part subject to any directions by the Attorney-General—
-- src:609 | about the matters set out in section 67:
-- src:610 | consistent with this Act and regulations made under this Act, about—
-- src:611 | the form in which legislation or consolidations of legislation (or any class of them) must be published (including the omission of signatures and formal or introductory parts); and
-- src:612 | any other matters concerning the publication of legislation or proposed legislation or minimum legislative information.
#ASSERT `the PCO must carry out its functions subject to the direction` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the PCO must carry out its functions subject to the direction` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the PCO must carry out its functions subject to the direction` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the PCO must carry out its functions subject to the direction` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- src:613 | A direction given by the Attorney-General under this Part must be given to the PCO in writing.
#ASSERT `the Attorney-General has given the direction as the Act requires` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the Attorney-General has given the direction as the Act requires` FALSE EQUALS FALSE

